Pipes
The pipe:
|&gt;
passes the result of one step into the next step.
Read it as:
then
Example:
recordTable |&gt;
  filter(Species == "White-tailed deer") |&gt;
  count(Station)

A complete pipeline

common_species &lt;- c(
  "White-tailed deer",
  "Armadillo",
  "Racoon",
  "Hog",
  "Virginia opossum"
)

common_summary &lt;- recordTable |&gt;
  filter(
    Species %in% common_species
  ) |&gt;
  group_by(Species) |&gt;
  summarise(
    records = n(),
    stations = n_distinct(Station),
    .groups = "drop"
  ) |&gt;
  arrange(
    desc(records)
  )

common_summary 

